        <Literal>Single-variant phenotype effects combine to give a double-variant effect different from the wild type and different from single variant effect. For instance, WT &lt; a = b &lt; ab, b &lt; WT = ab &lt; a, WT &lt; a &lt; b &lt; ab, b &lt; WT &lt; ab &lt; a, and all additional inequalities obtained by interchanging a and b, or reversing the effect of both a and b.</Literal>
